{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445993-help-me-design-a-kraina-for-denmark","id":1445993,"title":"Help me design a Kraina for Denmark","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-26T14:35:01-07:00","id":1445993,"title":"Help me design a Kraina for Denmark","content":"So im currently running a game set in the nation of denmark, and a plotpoint im doing is about a old clan tzimisce elder awakening from long gone torpor. He is a Wend, a slavic tribe that used to live on some of the southern danish islands. I want him to be a koldunist, and have a custom Kraina for the danish land. But im a bit at a loss for what powers would make sense.<br /> <br /> The general features of the danish terrain are the many small islands seperated by narrow belts of water. Long sandy beaches. Forests made of beach trees. The great heath on the western jutland peninsula, and the wadden sea to the west also.<br /> <br /> I want his powers to somewhat incorporate these elements, but at a bit of a loss where to start <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25428-ebtard","name":"Ebtard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T16:59:51-07:00","id":1446005,"title":"","content":"One easy place to start is looking at existing Koldunic powers, Kraina or otherwise, for inspiration. Or even powers from other Blood Sorcery Paths. It can give you a good guideline for how powerful each level of the Kraina should be. Sometimes it might be appropriate to just straight up steal an existing power and give it a local &quot;coat of paint.&quot; Other times it might just give you a rough idea that can then be tuned to the particulars of the geography or mythology that you're trying to represent.<br /> <br /> Another good source of inspiration is just reading about the local mythology or geography. I believe it was the main writer for the Kraina approach to Koldunism in DAV20 who mentioned that the &quot;Breath of Kupala&quot; power for the Transylvanian Kraina was based on the real-life existence of vast methane deposits beneath the region.<br /> <br /> PS Also, if you're talking about an Elder that learned Kraina during the Dark Medieval, make sure to check how the landscape compares between THEN and NOW. This actually made me ponder how radical changes in landscape might affect a Koldun's connection with the region that their Kraina come from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 04-26-2021, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T23:51:40-07:00","id":1446065,"title":"","content":"<br /> 1- you intimidate people with the amount of vowels you use<br /> 2-Icecream and hotdogs become extra delicious<br /> 3-liqourice becomes overly salted<br /> 4-armies of slugs assail you enemies. <br /> 5-you raise taxes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T03:46:13-07:00","id":1446089,"title":"","content":"So I followed Kharnovs advice, and looked through various koldunic sorcery ways and krainas, mix and matching and tweaking powers to suit the theme of the country. Taking inspiration from important features of the landscape and naturals disasters that have accured through history. I'll post what I came up with bellow. Any constructive critique of the rules I made is appreciated.<br /> <br /> <b>KRAINA OF DANIA<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">o - </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Near salty eastern shore</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A koldun invoking this power may command the sand of the nation to rise in a spray and crawl up a victim\u2019s legs. This power can command soil as well as sand, but not stone, and may only target victims standing on the earth. The kolduns of Denmark enjoy a special affinity to the sandy beaches that dominate the nation's coastlines. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">System:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The koldun spends a bloodpoint and rolls to activate the power (attribute: stamina) The koldun may then direct any patch of earth within a 100-foot/30-meter radius to ensnare a target for two turns per success rolled. Animated dirt ascends and constricts midway between the victim\u2019s knees and hips, holding her fast unless her player scores five successes on Strength + Survival roll (difficulty 6). </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is also possible to use this power as an attack, in which case the grasping earth crushes once and then releases. Used in this manner, each success on the casting inflicts one level of lethal damage. Such damage manifests as broken legs and crushed feet.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If used on the sand of any beach lining the danish coastline, this power requires no blood use.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">oo - </span></span><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It stands with broad beech-trees</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A koldun with this power commands nearby plants and trees to ensnare, and potentially immobilize their victims. This discipline affects plants of all sizes, compelling all from lowly heath stems, through beech branches and ancient twisting oak roots. Kolduns often use this power on plants surrounding paths leading to their havens.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>System:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The kolduns expends a blood point, ensuring the blood touches the plant she wishes to affect, and rolls to activate this power (Attribute: Dexterity). The plant will attempt to ensare anyone passing withing two meters (2 yards) of its reach, remaining ready to grapple this way for one night per blood point spent. For the purposes of grappling, the plant rolls six dice. It inflicts one level of bashing damage for each turn subsequent to a successful grapple. The plant gains an additional die to grappling with each subsequent turn, to a maximum of ten dice. Small plants possess two health levels for the purposes of destruction, with tree limbs holding up to six, depending on size. They hold one dot of stamina for each health level, and can soak bashing damage, with sufficiently thick tree limbs capable of soaking lethal damage.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If this power is used on a beech or oak tree within a danish forest, the plants\u2019 bashing damage and their health levels are doubled from their initial numbers, with stamina increasing as a byproduct of the increase in health.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">ooo - Embrace of the watery godshome</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Since ancient times, the mortals of the danish nation held the bogs and lakes that dot the landscape in reverence. Offering sacrifices of livestock and even humans to the deities and spirits they believed dwelled within. With this power, the koldun can assume the role of those terrible old spirits, submerging themselves in the ancient water and enjoying its protection.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>System:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The koldun must have access to a large enough body of water to submerge herself in. By splashing her blood into the body of water and making her activation roll (Attribute: Wits), she imbues that water with all the protective properties of a murky danish lake. She cannot be harmed by sunlight, her body is perfectly preserved for as long as she remains interred within, and she becomes extremely difficult to detect. To spot the koldun, a character must roll Perception + Alertness (difficulty 8) and achieve more successes than the koldun rolled on her activation roll. Those who engage the submerged Tzimisce take two levels of lethal damage each turn they remain in the freezing cold water.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When used in a danish bog or lake, this power requires no blood expenditure.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">oooo - And it is Frejas hall</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stories are rife with kolduns burying, drowning, or crushing helpless victims in the maw of the earth. Whether it is due to an innate innocence and purity of the land, or simply the twisted whims of the kolduns using it, this power manifests in a much more benevolent if still disturbing way. The soil ripples, parting and closing like some obscene womb as it draws the target a full yard beneath the surface. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Living beings entombed in this fashion do not suffocate, as the enchanted soil pumps air from above in undulating breaths. Better still, the fertile essence of the earth presses upon her flesh and restores it to new health. Still, the process is highly disturbing and unnatural, especially as targets remain wholly aware in silent, helpless immobility for the full duration. It is possible for a koldun to heal himself with</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">this power.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">System:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The player spends as many blood points as desired (which may require multiple turns depending on Generation) and makes the activation roll (Attribute: Stamina). Each success permits the earth to heal two levels of bashing damage or one level of lethal damage. Healing aggravated damage requires two successes per level. The total number of health levels that may be restored with each use of this power is the number of blood points invested or the number of successes on the activation roll, whichever is lower. Any blood points spent beyond the number of successes drain away to no effect. The actual healing process takes one turn per bashing level, one minute per lethal level, and one hour per aggravated level. Once the healing is complete or the power is interrupted through determined excavation, the earth expels the target back to the surface.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If used on earth within the traditional danish realm, from the Ejder to the forest border with G\u00f6taland, the used blood points count as double.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">ooooo - The great man-drowning</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The western coast along what the locals call the vadehav, or the wading sea, has always been a perilous place for settlement. The tides can manifest in great storm surges that historically have swallowed men, livestock, buildings and even entire islands into the sea. The deadliest of which were the great man-drownings of the 13. and 16. hundreds, which claimed thousands of humans lives across the jutland west coast.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>System:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With a successful activation roll (Attribute: Strength) and a point of Willpower (in addition to the usual blood), a koldun may conjure a terrible stormsurge. It takes six hours for the clouds to gather and thicken overhead, minus one hour for every success rolled. The storm persists at full strength for one hour per success rolled. It gradually dissipates over the hour following that.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The sea swells and surges forward, causing flooding of up to 1.5 meters in height (about 5 feet). Anyone, as well as most anything not secured to the ground, caught in its path will be swept away at a rate of a hundred yards a turn, and must soak six dice of bashing damage per turn. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Any subject somehow prevented from being carried downstream, wedged against a wall or other immovable object, for instance, takes twice the normal amount of damage.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Additionally, mortals must make a swimming roll (difficulty 8) each turn to avoid swallowing great mouthfuls of water; failure inflicts one additional level of lethal damage which cannot be soaked. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In addition, anyone caught in the winds of the storm suffers one die of bashing damage each turn (which may be soaked normally), loses two dice from all Dexterity pools, and moves at half normal speed.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25428,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25428-ebtard","user":"Ebtard","date":". 04-27-2021, 06:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25428-ebtard","name":"Ebtard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T10:26:11-07:00","id":1446117,"title":"","content":"I'm glad that my advice was helpful! Koldunism has been an interest of mine for a little while now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm not an expert on mechanics, and I'd have to do some checking, thinking, etc., before I could offer much advice on how balanced the powers are. I appreciate that you bumped Watery Godshome up to 3 dots in return for the added lethal damage. Great Man-Drowning looks like it mixes features from two different 5 dot powers; I'd have to check in more detail to see if you appropriately balanced that.<br /> <br /> The one thing I would perhaps recommend is changing either the 1 dot or 2 dot power. You have two levels in a row where the power is &quot;grapple someone with nature.&quot; Just a bit redundant, IMO.<br /> <br /> For an NPC Elder, this seems like a decent kraina at first glance <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T13:09:26-07:00","id":1446138,"title":"","content":"Heh, turning the national anthem into a kraina. I approve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T22:39:33-07:00","id":1446562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445993-help-me-design-a-kraina-for-denmark?p=1446065#post1446065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- you intimidate people with the amount of vowels you use<br /> 2-Icecream and hotdogs become extra delicious<br /> 3-liqourice becomes overly salted<br /> 4-armies of slugs assail you enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having lived most of my young life in Helsingborg (which is a stone's throw from the Danish town of Helsing\u00f6r, if you have a good Catapult or Trebuchet, that is) - I strongly support these 4 listed. Oh my god the danish p\u00f6lse/hot dogs are delicious and their icecream is to kill for. And even though i have lived that near (about 20 min wiith commercial ferry between the ports9 - understanding danish vowel use is beyond most sane people.<br /> <br /> I have heard a rumour that the first danish people met with Chhutulu at the begining of time and his presence made the entire line of descendants go insane and talking jibberish.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T06:12:56-07:00","id":1446590,"title":"","content":"Wh\u00e5t d\u00f8 you m\u00e6n, Danish v\u00f8wels are difficult?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}